/*
 * Sophon on the XIAO nRF54LM20A Sense (#370; the rest of this board's
 * devicetree arrives with the direct-role port, NRF54LM20A-PLAN.md Phase 3).
 *
 * THE CLOCK NODES THE BOARD FILE LEAVES OFF.
 *
 * Zephyr's boards/seeed/xiao_nrf54lm20a (at 4.4.99, 2026-08-08) enables the
 * SoC's `lfxo` and `hfxo` but none of the nodes this Zephyr's clock driver
 * uses: `xo`, `lfclk` and `xo24m`, all `status = "disabled"` in
 * nrf54lm20_a_b.dtsi. The Bluetooth controller looks up an enabled
 * `nordic,nrf-clock-lfclk` for its sleep-clock accuracy (lll_clock.c,
 * DT_COMPAT_GET_ANY_STATUS_OKAY), finds none, and fails to COMPILE:
 *
 *     error: '__P_k32src_accuracy_ppm_IDX_0_ENUM_IDX' undeclared
 *
 * So no Bluetooth application builds for this board -- Zephyr's own
 * samples/bluetooth/peripheral included, unmodified (#370). Nordic's
 * nrf54lm20dk enables exactly these three; doing the same here fixes the build.
 *
 * `lfclk` keeps its binding defaults: k32src "xtal", 50 ppm. The board has a
 * 32.768 kHz crystal (X1, 7 pF, +/-20 ppm, per the KiCad V1.0 schematic), so a
 * crystal source and a 50 ppm accuracy class are both honest.
 *
 * To be removed once the board file is fixed upstream.
 */

&xo {
	status = "okay";
};

&lfclk {
	status = "okay";
};

&xo24m {
	status = "okay";
};
